7036 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 586 0 R/E(Attending school on time is important for a successful learning experience. Showing respect to your teacher creates a positive classroom environment. Sitting peacefully like attentive students helps you and others focus better. Always ask for permission before leaving the room. After school, it's a good habit to head straight home. Avoid any conflicts with others on your way back. Education is a valuable virtue that serves you well in life. Engage deeply with your studies and strive for clarity. Practice writing with care, as it can lead to becoming a skilled writer. Maintain a proper distance from books to protect your eyes. After your lessons, focus on memorizing them thoroughly. Continue studying at home to reinforce your learning. Reading while lying down can strain your eyes, so always read while sitting upright. Appreciate anyone who teaches you, no matter how small the lesson.)/Pg 166 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

