7058 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 589 0 R/E(Whatever we eat, it gives strength to our body. Before eating, wash your hands and face. Take small bites and eat by chewing thoroughly. Do not eat without hunger. Even when feeling hungry, do not eat more food than the body's need out of greed. By eating too much and by eating all the time, the body catches many diseases. Only by eating according to the body's need does the body remain healthy. Do not eat too many hot spices, very hot things, or things with a very hot nature. By eating such things, many diseases occur inside the stomach.)/Pg 169 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

7059 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 589 0 R/E(Consume whatever thing is suitable for the body or the stomach. While starting to consume any thing, consume it by saying Vaheguru. After eating, definitely rinse your mouth. If possible, then give some of your food to someone else as well. Sharing and eating is a supreme virtue. Do not eat leftovers \(Jutha\); by eating leftovers, many illnesses are caught, and do not be greedy for any thing.)/Pg 169 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

