endobj

7086 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 591 0 R/E(Whatever you speak, speak thoughtfully and speak the truth; do not speak in vain or without a purpose. Do not tell lies. Telling lies is a sin. If someone is talking, you should not speak in the middle of it. Do not interrupt another's conversation. Do not speak too loudly, such that it causes distress to anyone. Do not make fun of elders. Call them with respect and honor by saying 'Ji'. Call youngsters with love as well. If you joke with your peers, let it be such that no one feels hurt upon hearing it. Do not let your mind be enticed by another's property. Never even entertain the thought in your mind of stealing or snatching it. In this way, bad habits are formed. Through bad deeds like stealing, a person's merits \(good deeds\) decrease. If you find someone's belonging, return it to them.)/Pg 171 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

